SUMMARY:Village Dance - Spring Edition
DESCRIPTION:Village Dance – Spring Edition\nThursday\, May 21\, 2026\n6:15pm – 9:30pm \nVets Memorial\n203 14th st.\, Davis\, CA\nGet your tickets in advance here (our venue is requesting a guest list in advance)\nVillage Dance is a somatic journey through music and movement. We strive to co-create an inclusive space for everybody. To create a meditative environment\, we ask that the dance floor remains shoe-free\, conversation-free and substance-free. Please arrive on time to experience the whole event! As always\, we are incredibly grateful for all the hands that make this event possible!\nSchedule: \n6:15pm – Doors Open\n6:30pm – Opening Workshop with Tamara Vodovoz\n7:00pm – Dance Journey with Lil Fish\n9:00pm – Closing Circle \nTamara @tamaravodovozyoga\nLil Fish @lilfishmusic \nLil Fish\nLil Fish is a French DJ and electronic music producer whose\nsonic universe continues to expand over the years.\nHe skillfully navigates between tracks tailored for the dancefloor—\ndriven by powerful\, melodious\, and organic bass music—and\nmore introspective\, mid-tempo compositions that immerse the\nlistener in dark\, raw\, and emotionally deep atmospheres.\nWhat truly sets Lil Fish apart is his unique ability to blend modern\nrhythms with traditional sounds from Asia or Eastern Europe. This\nfusion invites us on a genuine mystical and sensory journey\,\noscillating between light and darkness\, tribal energy and\nmeditative reverie. \nTamara Vodovoz\nTamara\, originally from Colombia\, pursued her passion for the well-being of living beings through Veterinary Medicine. Her academic journey took her to the University of California\, Davis\, where she earned a master’s and Ph.D. in epidemiology and Comparative Pathology.\nSimultaneously\, Tamara has been a dedicated yoga student since her teenage years and a teacher for the past 13 years\, advocating for the profound benefits of yoga for individuals from all walks of life. As a yoga instructor\, she blends scientific understanding with holistic approaches\, incorporating myofascial release\, nervous system regulation\, and self-massage techniques.\nTamara is also very enthusiastic about Thai massage\, a partner practice emphasizing the Buddhist concept of Metta (loving kindness) to heal our sense of separation and co-regulate emotions. She has been studying Thai Massage since 2010\, traveling to Thailand and studying with inspiring teachers. She has been offering traditional Thai Massage and table Thai massage at Dynamics Davis since 2018.\nHer journey reflects a blend of scientific inquiry\, spiritual exploration\, and a commitment to fostering interconnectedness. Through her work and teachings\, Tamara inspires others to deepen their connection with themselves and the world.\nCurrent public Yoga classes at Yoga Yolo studio\, private yoga and Thai massage at www.tamaravodovoz.com
URL:https://thedirt.online/event/village-dance-spring-edition/
LOCATION:Davis Veterans Memorial Center\, 203 East 14th Street\, Davis\, CA\, 95616
CATEGORIES:Community,Music,Stage & Dance
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://thedirt.online/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/vdmay2026.jpeg
ORGANIZER;CN="Village Dance Davis":MAILTO:dmoglen@gmail.com
END:VEVENT
